<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Oreshek Fortress</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1323</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Oreshek, Shlisselburg Fortress, Nöteborg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Oreshek is a fortress on an island at the source of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neva-river">Neva River</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-ladoga">Lake Ladoga</a>, founded by Novgorod in 1323. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-noteborg">Treaty of Nöteborg</a>, the first border agreement between Novgorod and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>, was signed there the same year. Held by Sweden as Nöteborg from 1612, it was taken by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-the-great">Peter the Great</a> in 1702 and renamed Shlisselburg, later serving as a notorious political prison.</p></div>
